AirDrop support is coming to Samsung's Quick Share feature on Galaxy S26 devices this week, allowing owners to directly share files and media with iPhones and Macs.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/samsung-galaxy-s26-new-purple.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1037826" /><br/>
In a Sunday <a href="https://news.samsung.com/us/samsung-airdrop-quick-share-galaxy-s26-series/?utm_source=pr_media&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=generalhttps://news.samsung.com/us/samsung-airdrop-quick-share-galaxy-s26-series/">newsroom announcement</a>, Samsung said the rollout is starting today in Korea, with devices in the U.S. to follow later this week. The feature will expand to more regions and on more Galaxy devices at a later date, including Canada, Latin America, Europe, Southeast Asia, Hong Kong, Japan, and Taiwan.<br/>
<br/>
Owners of Galaxy S26, S26 Plus, and S26 Ultra devices will need to enable the feature in their phone's Quick Share settings menu, using a new Share with Apple devices toggle.<br/>
<br/>
